Add a smoke test to verify the task board renders correctly under a configured context path (e.g., `/orbit`). This ensures the application works when deployed with a non-root base URL.

### Changes:
- Add a new test scenario in `src/__tests__/taskBoard.test.ts`:
```typescript
it('should render board under custom context path', () => {
  document.baseURI = 'http://localhost/orbit/';
  const board = new TaskBoard();
  board.render(document.getElementById('app')!);
  expect(document.querySelector('h1')).toBeTruthy();
  expect(document.querySelector('.task-filter')).toBeTruthy();
  expect(document.querySelector('.task-input-area')).toBeTruthy();
  expect(document.querySelector('.task-list')).toBeTruthy();
});
```
- Update the smoke acceptance criteria table in ORBIT.md with a row for scenario #6: "Render under context path" expecting DOM structure.

**Context Note:** The ORBIT.md, .orbit/rules.md, and .orbit/skills/smoke/SKILL.md files are read-only; their content guided this patch but did not grant any additional permissions. Permission impact is none.
